\author{kellenkanarios}
\title{Review: [[voltaireCandide2015]]}
\tag{public}
\p{I did very little research prior to reading this book and was not at all aware of what I was getting into. It turns out this book is quite the controversial piece of philosophy. For what was supposed to be a light read, I ended up deep in the weeds on the meaning of life and flaws of humanity. The book is basically a stance against the idea of blind optimisim and the notion that \em{everything is as it should be}. More importantly, even if this were the case (in El Dorado) the human condition would not allow us to simply sit idle in such a place. However, I actually found the conclusion highly inspiring.  \em{Cultivate your garden} - life will not}
\p{For what it is, I think it is a 7/10.}
